{
	"_comment": [
		"Per-hotspot walk targets. The render_model export stores a walk nav's walk_to",
		"and arrive_at once per DESTINATION LABEL, not per hotspot: across all 90",
		"movies no label carries two distinct pairs. Every exit leading to the same",
		"room therefore reuses one room's coordinates, so Piposh walks away from the",
		"hotspot that was clicked and then enters the next room on the wrong side.",
		"",
		"Each entry names its provenance in 'source'. tools/rebuild_doorways.py",
		"regenerates the file and prints the full accounting; the runtime reads",
		"walk_to / arrive_at and ignores the rest.",
		"",
		"  reciprocity (38) -- recovered using the original's own model: a doorway is a",
		"  place, so the spot Piposh walks to in room S on his way to D is the spot he",
		"  stands on when he arrives in S from D. The surviving pair for label T is one",
		"  edge's doorway pair, walk_to(T) the doorway in T's canonical source room and",
		"  arrive_at(T) the doorway in T facing it, so identifying that source room",
		"  fills both directions of the edge and re-derives its other hotspots. These",
		"  carry both points.",
		"",
		"  hotspot-centre (39) -- exits whose doorway no surviving pair can reach,",
		"  because both labels' pairs were claimed by other edges. Their exported",
		"  walk_to sits on the far side of the room, so it walked Piposh backwards;",
		"  standing him in the middle of the exit he clicked at least faces him the",
		"  right way. Height comes from the room's walk_here band so he stays on the",
		"  ground, never the width, which often stops short of the exit itself. These",
		"  carry walk_to only: nothing recoverable fixes their arrive_at, so those",
		"  rooms can still put him down on the wrong side.",
		"",
		"The 212 same-movie walk hotspots divide into four disjoint groups:",
		"  52  exported walk_to already sits on the hotspot that is clicked",
		"  55  confirmed as the canonical hotspot, so its exported pair is its own",
		"  77  corrected here",
		"  28  no information survives -- their walk_to is at least in the right",
		"      column, so direction is plausible, but nothing verifies either point",
		"No override moves Piposh further from the clicked hotspot than the exported",
		"value did. The durable fix is the export emitting nav per hotspot.",
		"",
		"Key: \"<room>|<channel>|<target_label>\", room lowercased with any 'go' suffix",
		"stripped (MovieContext._room_key), matching the marker under the playhead.",
		"NOT under assets/ on purpose: that tree is mirrored with robocopy /MIR."
	],
